  "text": "proprium.vigilia-nativitatis-introitus",
  "about": "The introitus of the formulary “Vigil of the Nativity of the Lord” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Today ye shall know that the Lord will come and save us, and in the morning ye shall see His glory. The earth is the Lord’s and the fullness thereof, the world and all that dwell therein. Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Ghost. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen. Today ye shall know that the Lord will come and save us, and in the morning ye shall see His glory." }
